enue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a32.9m planned development of Cannon Public House cancelled; property now held for sale","lead":"Signals a shift in council investment strategy; conversion of development asset to sale removes planned future capital release and suggests development challenges","iso":"2026-07-13","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-13","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","headline":"Usable capital reserves forecast to decline 84% over three years, from \u00a330.8m to \u00a35.1m","detail":"Capital receipts and grants will be depleted significantly over the 2026/27 to 2027/28 period due to committed capital spending, declining from \u00a330.8m to \u00a35.1m. Report notes that this projection excludes uncertainty around receipts from Dove Lane sale.","category":"capital","matters":"Sharp decline in capital funding capacity constrains ability to fund future capital without increased borrowing or reserves depletion; uncertainty about Dove Lane adds execution risk","figures":"Capital reserves: \u00a330,766k (2025/26) declining to \u00a35,065k (2027/28), 84% reduction","quote":"usable capital reserve balances dropping significantly over the period due to existing commitments","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-13","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","headline":"Council carries \u00a326.3m of unfunded capital spend funded through internal borrowing against cash balances","detail":"The council has no external borrowing but holds a Capital Financing Requirement (CFR) of \u00a326.3m related to previous unfunded capital investments (including Platinum Stages and loans to subsidiary companies). This is funded by drawing on internal cash balances rather than external borrowing.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Significant internal borrowing constrains future borrowing capacity and ties up cash reserves that could provide liquidity buffer; indicates previous capital decisions created ongoing funding gaps","figures":"\u00a326,301k CFR, no external borrowing","quote":"a need to borrow of \u00a326,301k (also known as the Capital Financing Requirement or CFR) which is in relation to previous unfunded capital spend, such as the Platinum Stages and loans to subsidiary and related companies","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-13","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","headline":"\u00a32.9m planned development of Cannon Public House cancelled; property now held for sale","detail":"A capital investment of \u00a32.9m in developing a public house property has been withdrawn. The council is now selling the asset rather than completing the development.","category":"capital","matters":"Signals a shift in council investment strategy; conversion of development asset to sale removes planned future capital release and suggests development challenges","figures":"\u00a32,937k","quote":"\u00a32,937k Cannon Public House: development no longer going ahead, now held for sale.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-13","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","headline":"\u00a315.9m capital spending deferred to future years, equal to 57% of this year's planned budget","detail":"Capital spend was \u00a38.5m against revised budget of \u00a328.2m, with \u00a315.9m slippage to future years. Major deferrals include: Catterick Way \u00a33.2m, CIL-funded projects \u00a33.6m, parks projects \u00a32.9m, Darkes Lane \u00a32.3m (being rescoped), temporary accommodation \u00a30.5m. Projects now concentrated in 2026/27 onwards.","category":"capital","matters":"Large-scale, sustained capital slippage suggests project delivery challenges; future years will face concentrated spending demands and potential funding pressure","figures":"\u00a315,964k slippage, \u00a328,214k revised budget, \u00a33,243k Catterick Way, \u00a33,641k CIL projects, \u00a32,913k parks, \u00a32,344k Darkes Lane","quote":"The year-end variance of \u00a319,740k includes project slippage which will be re-profiled in the capital programme to future years totalling \u00a315,964k, under spends amounting to \u00a33,895k and an overspend of (\u00a3119k).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-13","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"20260713CAB-CAB26127- Revenue and Capital Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://hertsmere.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72943/72943.pdf","headline":"Rental income from key council assets fell \u00a31.3m due to asbestos remediation and tenant departure","detail":"Asset Management shows \u00a31,427k deficit. Elstree Film Studios rent was cut by \u00a3300k due to asbestos remediation; Platinum Stages lost \u00a3957k when a tenant used a break clause in July 2025. A new tenant was secured in June 2026, with recovery to budget level (\u00a31.7m) expected for 2026/27.","category":"income","matters":"Material loss of revenue income from commercial assets directly affects council's financial resilience and ability to invest in services","figures":"\u00a31,427k deficit, \u00a31,257k total shortfall, \u00a3300k from Studios, \u00a3957k from Platinum Stages","quote":"there was a loss of (\u00a3957k) from the Platinum Stages following the departure of the original tenant in July 2025, the tenant having initiated the three-year break clause in their agreement.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-14"},"name":"Hertsmere","findings_total":46,"news_drafts_total":3}}